1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Times 11?
Split and add!

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,470
What is 23 × 11?
In your head, in 6 seconds!

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:10,470
Can you do it without writing it out?

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,440
Split the two digits apart

5
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:14,410
In the middle goes their sum:
2 + 3 = 5

6
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,630
23 × 11 = 253!

7
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:22,400
Your turn! What is 62 × 11?

8
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:25,770
6 | 6+2 | 2 → 682!

9
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,940
Because 11 is 10 + 1

10
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:29,710
23 × 10 = 230

11
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,680
23 × 1 = 23, shifted over one place

12
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:33,500
Add them in columns…

13
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:37,470
Only the middle place is 2 + 3!
That's why it's split and add

14
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:40,010
What if the sum is over 10, like 57 × 11?

15
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:44,280
Carry the 1 to the front → 627

16
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:46,930
Quiz your mom and dad!

17
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,630
3 tricks —
who will you try them on?
